INT. ABANDONED CARNIVAL HOUSE OF MIRRORS - NIGHT

Cracked glass everywhere. A flashlight beam jitters across a hundred reflections.

MARISOL QUINTANA (20s, hoodie, camera on a strap) walks backward, panning. Her sister CATALINA QUINTANA (20s, same hoodie, different colour) holds the light.

Between them, LIAM FAIRWEATHER (20s, rental-car keys in a fist) steps on glass and swears under his breath.

MARISOL
Stay close.

CATALINA
I am close.

LIAM
She's closer than you.

Something thumps on the other side of the glass. All three freeze. Catalina swings the light. Nothing. Only their own faces, split into pieces.

MARISOL
(whispering)
Count.

CATALINA
Three.

LIAM
Count the reflections.

She does. Her lips move. She gets to a number and stops.

A breath, not theirs, fogs the mirror at the end of the corridor. A shape steps out of it that is not one of them.

Marisol lifts the camera. Her hands don't shake. She presses record.

Liam drops the keys. They ring on the floor like a bell.

The light dies.

CUT TO BLACK.
